1. Full Automated Issue → Diagnosis → Fix Workflow

After the POC, the system can be expanded to perform:

Multi-step troubleshooting flows

Automated diagnosis using historical patterns

Automatic selection of the best remediation workflow

End-to-end execution with zero human intervention

This will enable Level–1 and Level–2 issue resolution to be fully automated.

2. Dynamic Runbook Generation

Instead of cloning existing runbooks only, the system can:

Generate new runbooks dynamically using AI

Modify logic based on system context

Create tailored automation steps per server/application

This moves the platform toward auto-generated remediation playbooks.

3. Full ServiceNow Integration

After the POC, these can be added:

Auto-create incidents

Auto-update ticket status

Auto-close tickets after runbook success

Two-way syncing with assignment groups, CMDB, CI mappings

This creates a closed-loop ITSM automation pipeline.

4. SCCM / Intune Remediation Workflows

Once basic SCCM connectivity is validated in the POC:

Patch installation workflows

Software deployment automation

Compliance remediation

System restart/health checks

Application-specific fixes

This brings real operational automation to desktop/server environments.

5. AI-powered Root Cause Analysis

After POC, the system can:

Analyze logs, events, metrics

Detect anomalies across systems

Correlate issues (SCCM, SNOW, DataPower, etc.)

Recommend preventive actions

This establishes Predictive Operations (AIOps).

6. Multi-Agent Conversational Troubleshooting

Future work can include:

Tier-1 virtual agent for basic diagnosis

Tier-2 reasoning agent for deep troubleshooting

Runbook agent for execution

Knowledge agent for documentation search

This will build a full agentic ecosystem for IT support.

7. Cross-Platform Automation

With the foundation built in the POC, you can automate flows across:

Azure

On-prem servers via Hybrid Runbook Worker

SCCM

DataPower

WebMethods

ServiceNow

Azure Arc managed servers

This becomes a single unified automation platform.

8. Real-Time Telemetry & Dashboarding

You can add:

Automated dashboards from Event Hub

Runbook success/failure metrics

MTTR reduction analysis

AI reasoning traceability

This delivers strong observability & governance.

9. Enterprise Governance (Phase-2)

Future enhancements include:

Role-based execution approvals

Change management integration

Production-ready security

Runbook version governance

Automated rollback tasks

This makes the solution enterprise compliant.

10. Large-Scale Rollout Across Use Cases

This POC can be extended to cover:

Windows/Linux troubleshooting

Patching

Database checks

Network validation

App-server restart workflows

Health checks

Compliance management

This evolves into a smart automation command center.
